# The Sunsword speaking while somebody carries it (NPC plan Part D; docs/story/the_sunsword.md): short lines in the guest-banter
# format (story/banter.gd treats the blade as a guest while it is carried, and its idle_stash lines play while it lies in the
# stash). The node's name says when it may play: quest_ on entering an area, place_ on entering one, fight_ after a won fight,
# idle_ now and then on the road. Each plays once per playthrough. Every line here is unvoiced for now. Its words in a fight
# are in narrative/narrator/sunsword.dialogue, and in the count's scenes in the scenes' own files.

~ quest_found
if item:sunsword and not flag.sunsword_woke
set sunsword_woke
Sunsword: At last. You have kept me in the dark for a very dull hour, friend, and the dust on my pommel is a disgrace.
Sunsword: Stand straight when you hold me. A prince's hilt is not a walking stick, and your grip is abominably slack.
Sunsword: Where is Sergei? Tell him the elder brother has had his little tantrum, and I require a smith of the first rank.
Sunsword [weary]: Do not stare at me as though I were a turnip that had learned to sing. Tell me the year, and speak clearly.
endif
-> END

~ quest_attune
if item:sunsword and flag.sunsword_woke and not flag.sunsword_attuned
set sunsword_attuned
Sunsword [smile]: Very well, I accept your service. Your lineage is obscure and your posture is tragic, yet we shall manage.
Sunsword: Observe the blade: pure dawn, without need of steel or stone. You may admire it now, to save us time on the road.
Sunsword: Our business is simple. We shall find every leech in this valley and turn them to ash before the soup grows cold.
Sunsword: I expect brisk marching, dry scabbards, and strict punctuality. Dawdling is a vice I do not forgive in a squire.
endif
-> END

~ place_pool
if item:sunsword and at:krezk_pool_of_the_white_sun
Sunsword: Hold a moment. I know this water, and the white light that sleeps at the bottom of it.
Sunsword: Sergei knelt on these stones before the wedding was even spoken of. The water was warmer then, or perhaps I was.
Sunsword [sad]: Do not dip me in it. Let the pool keep the memory it has of him, when I still had my crystal whole.
endif
-> END

~ place_tomb
if item:sunsword and at:castle_ravenloft_catacombs_tombs
Sunsword [sad]: Be quiet here. Lower my light, if you know how, and take your hand from the pommel for a little while.
Sunsword [sad]: Good evening, my prince. I am very late, and I have brought a stranger, but I have not forgotten our errand.
endif
-> END

~ place_holt
if item:sunsword and region:argynvostholt
Sunsword: The Silver Dragon's hall. In my day their armour shone so fiercely I considered them rivals, though naturally they came second.
Sunsword: Walk with some dignity among these stones. They died standing up against the elder brother, which is more than most managed.
endif
-> END

~ place_castle
if item:sunsword and region:castle_ravenloft
Sunsword: So the elder brother has kept the towers standing. He always had a taste for cold stone and long shadows.
Sunsword: There were banners in this courtyard once, gold and crimson, and music loud enough to drown the wind from the drop.
Sunsword [afraid]: Keep your both hands on my grip as we cross the threshold. The stone here remembers how a blade is broken.
endif
-> END

~ fight_first
if item:sunsword and not flag.sunsword_first_fight
set sunsword_first_fight
Sunsword [smile]: Make way, make way! The morning has arrived, and it is in a foul temper.
Sunsword: Hold your wrist firm and try not to embarrass us, squire. I shall do the real work.
endif
-> END

~ fight_ashes
if item:sunsword and flag.sunsword_first_fight and (region:argynvostholt or region:castle_ravenloft or region:death_house)
Sunsword: Ashes to ashes, and good riddance to cheap rot. Four centuries of waiting, and it still feels like a holiday.
Sunsword: Wipe the hilt, if you please. Even a corpse that turns to dust leaves a smear on good silver.
endif
-> END

~ fight_after_1
if item:sunsword and flag.sunsword_first_fight
Sunsword: Do wipe your sleeves before you sheathe me. I have no wish to smell of whatever that was.
Sunsword: Still, your footwork was almost courtly on the third lunge. Almost.
endif
-> END

~ fight_after_2
if item:sunsword and flag.sunsword_first_fight
Sunsword: That is how matters were settled in Sergei's day: brightly, briefly, and without all this slouching.
endif
-> END

~ fight_undead
if item:sunsword and (region:argynvostholt or region:castle_ravenloft or region:death_house)
Sunsword: Ah, how cleanly they go to ash! That is the work I was forged to do, and I do it handsomely.
Sunsword: Keep that iron stick in your belt next time. They deserve a proper sunrise at the end.
endif
-> END

~ idle_dawdle
if item:sunsword
Sunsword: Are we taking root, squire, or merely waiting for the moss to climb our boots? The road goes forward.
Sunsword: At this pace the elder brother will die of old age, which would be a theological miracle and a personal insult to me.
endif
-> END

~ idle_shops
if item:sunsword
Sunsword [weary]: Salt pork, hemp rope, and three kinds of tallow. Clearly this is the grand crusade for which I was forged.
Sunsword: If you haggle over one more copper piece, I shall shine directly into the merchant's eyes until we are both thrown out.
endif
-> END

~ idle_weapons
if item:sunsword
Sunsword: Must I travel beside that notched iron stick at your companion's hip? It looks as though it were hammered out of a kettle.
Sunsword: Tell the one with the little bread knife to stand downwind. Rusty steel gives me the most dreadful headache.
endif
-> END

~ idle_light
if item:sunsword
Sunsword [smile]: Take note of how the mist parts when I am bare. Even the weather in this miserable ditch knows its betters.
Sunsword: A lesser blade gleams; I preside. Try to look a little more heroic in my glow, for the sake of the composition.
endif
-> END

~ idle_ireena
if item:sunsword and guest:ireena
Sunsword [smile]: Lady Ireena, if my glare offends your eyes upon the road, say the word and I shall dim myself to a lantern.
Sunsword: You have the very step of one who used to walk the castle gardens when the roses still had colour.
Sunsword [sad]: Walk close beside my bearer, my lady: I was forged to keep the dark from touching hair like yours.
endif
-> END

~ idle_running
if item:sunsword and attention >= marked
Sunsword [angry]: Your heels are pointed the wrong way, bearer: the elder brother is behind us, and my light does not shine backward.
Sunsword: Turn about and plant your boots, I say, for I did not wait four centuries to watch a vampire's cloak from a sprint.
endif
-> END

~ idle_stash
Sunsword [angry]: I am the royal blade of Prince Sergei von Zarovich, currently keeping company with a salt herring and three spare boots.
Sunsword: Take me out of this sack at once, before you go into battle armed with that dreary iron stick.
-> END
